  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This problem has the same setup and definitions as MINMEXSUM. However, they differ in what needs to be computed, as well as the constraint on NNN.**\n\nConsider a tree on NNN vertices, with vertex uuu having value AuA_uAu​ written on it.\n\nWe have the following definitions:\n\n\nFor two vertices u,vu, vu,v, define P(u,v)P(u, v)P(u,v) to be the set of vertices on the unique simple path from uuu to vvv in the tree.\nDefine mn(u,v)\\text{mn}(u, v)mn(u,v) to be the minimum value of AwA_wAw​ across all w∈P(u,v)w \\in P(u, v)w∈P(u,v), that is, mn(u,v)\\text{mn}(u, v)mn(u,v) is the minimum value on the path between uuu and vvv.\nS={mn(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N}S = \\{ \\text{mn}(u, v) \\mid 1 \\leq u \\lt v \\leq N \\}S={mn(u,v)∣1≤u&lt;v≤N}, i.e. SSS is the set of all path minimums of the tree, excluding paths consisting of a single vertex.\nWe then define score(A)\\text{score}(A)score(A) to be the smallest **positive** integer that doesn't appear in SSS.\n\nIn simpler words, score(A)\\text{score}(A)score(A) is the smallest positive integer that doesn't appear as the minimum of any path in the tree, when only considering paths with length at least 222.\n\nYou are given a tree on NNN vertices, and an array AAA.\n\nEach element of AAA is an integer in the range [0,N][0, N][0,N]. It is guaranteed that the non-zero elements of AAA are pairwise distinct.\n\nYou would like to replace **every** 000 in AAA with an integer in [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nThe elements of AAA must remain distinct after replacement, i.e. the final array should be a permutation of {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N}.\n\nCompute the **minimum** possible value score(A)\\text{score}(A)score(A) can attain.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of vertices.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges of the tree. The iii-th of them contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between these two vertices.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum possible value of score(A)\\text{score}(A)score(A).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
